## How many employees leave the company?
SQL query :
SELECT
COUNT(*) AS totalEmployee,
SUM(CASE WHEN Attrition=TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS employeeLeft,
ROUND((SUM(CASE WHEN Attrition=TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)/COUNT(*))*100,2) AS attritionRate
FROM `hr-attrition-and-performance.hrData.data`
Result :
totalEmployee = 1470
employeeLeft = 237
attritionRate = 16.12

## Which department is losing the most talent?
SQL query :
SELECT
Department,
COUNT(*) AS totalEmployee,
SUM(CASE WHEN Attrition = TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS totalAttrition,
ROUND((SUM(CASE WHEN Attrition = TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)/COUNT(*))*100,2) AS attritionRate
FROM `hr-attrition-and-performance.hrData.data`
GROUP BY Department
ORDER BY ROUND((SUM(CASE WHEN Attrition = TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)/COUNT(*))*100,2) DESC
Result :
Sales -> totalEmployee 446, totalAttrition 92, attritionRate 20.63

